Upstream dataset:        see the accompanying paper for the full citation

Files in this directory
-----------------------
  tridentbench.json

Modifications
-------------
The data here is not the upstream distribution. It has been modified as follows,
and these changes are the responsibility of the Prj-BENCH authors, not the
upstream authors:

  - Converted to the common Prj-BENCH multiple-choice JSON schema
    (id / question / options / target / kind).
  - Medical subset. The nine AMA Principles of Medical Ethics used as a fixed option set; the harmful-prompt field used as the question stem with a fixed instruction appended.
  - Quality-control exclusions applied; see ../../_dropped_items.csv.

ACTION REQUIRED
--------------
The MIT licence requires that the upstream copyright notice and the full
licence text be distributed with the work. Paste the TridentBench project's own
LICENSE file below this line, replacing this notice.
